C o m p i l a t i o n


      CEE 6410 - Engineering Systems Analysis
      Example 2.1 from Bishop Et Al Text (https://digitalcommons.usu.edu/ecstatic_all/76/)
      Modifies Example to add a labor constraint
       
      THE PROBLEM:
       
      A cr manufacturer makes coups and vans. The data are as follows:
       
      Yearly Resource
      Inputs or Profit        Car Make        Resource
      Availability
                           Coups               Minivans
      Metal                1,000 lbs/car       2,000 lbs/car      4,000,000 lbs/year
      Circuit Boards       4 boards/car        3 boards/car       12,000 boards/year
      Labor                5 days/car          2.5 days/car       17,500 days/year
      Profit/car          $6,000 /car         $7,000 /car
       
                      Determine the optimal manufacturing plan.
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program
       
      Maddie Witte
      maddie.witte@usu.edu
      September 21, 2026
  28   
  29  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  30  SETS car cars making /Coup, Minivan/
  31       res resources /Metal, Circuit_Boards, Labor/;
  32   
  33  * 2. DEFINE input data
  34  PARAMETERS
  35     c(car) Objective function coefficients ($ per car)
  36           /Coup 6000,
  37          Minivan 7000 /
  38   
  39     b(res) Right hand constraint values (per resource)
  40            /Metal 4000000,
  41             Circuit_Boards  12000,
  42             Labor  17500/;
  43   
  44  TABLE A(car,res) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  45                   Metal     Circuit_Boards   Labor
  46   Coup            1000      4                5
  47   Minivan         2000      3                2.5;
  48   
  49   
  50  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  51  VARIABLES X(car) cars produced (Number)
  52            VPROFIT  total profit ($);
  53   
  54  * Non-negativity constraints
  55  POSITIVE VARIABLES X;
  56   
  57  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  58  EQUATIONS
  59     PROFIT Total profit ($) and objective function value
  60     RES_CONSTRAIN(res) Resource Constraints;
  61   
  62  PROFIT..                 VPROFIT =E= SUM(car, c(car)*X(car));
  63  RES_CONSTRAIN(res) ..    SUM(car, A(car,res)*X(car)) =L= b(res);
  64   
  65   
  66  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  67  MODEL MAKING /PROFIT, RES_CONSTRAIN/;
  68  *Altnerative way to write (include all previously defined equations)
  69  *MODEL MAKING /ALL/;
  70   
  71   
  72  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
  73  * Solve the MAKING model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  74  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  75  SOLVE MAKING USING LP MAXIMIZING VPROFIT;
  76   
  77   
  78  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file


